    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240-a1">

                <pb facs="0298" n="248" xml:id="pg248"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 294.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Roosevelt to Lord Kimberley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-23"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to Mr. Bayard’s note of
                    August 16, 1894, to your predecessor, and in accordance with instructions from
                    my Government, I have the honor to ask your Lordship to be so good as to permit
                    the newly appointed British agent and consul-general at Sofia to continue the
                    good offices heretofore extended, so courteously and efficiently, to citizens of
                    the United States by his predecessor in office, Mr. Dering.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James R.
                    Roosevelt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
